# detector-geometry-sources

**WCSim geometry dumps** for Super-K, Hyper-K (hybrid mPMT + OD) and the NuPRISM beam test. These are
the only input to `scripts/geofile_to_npz.py`, which produced the tracked
`sk_geometry.npz` / `hk_geometry.npz` / `wcte_geometry.npz` — nothing in `lucid/` reads them.
Regenerate with `python scripts/geofile_to_npz.py <geofile> <out.npz>`. `docs/guides/model-your-own-detector.md`
cites `geofile_SuperK.txt` literally, so that page points here.

## What is in this tarball

| path | size at this commit | produced |
|---|---|---|
| `config/geofile_HyperK_HybridmPMT_WithOD_Realistic.txt` | 4.1 MB | `hk_geometry.npz` |
| `config/geofile_SuperK.txt` | 1.2 MB | `sk_geometry.npz` |
| `config/geofile_NuPRISMBeamTest_16cShort_mPMT.txt` | 216 KB | `wcte_geometry.npz` |
| `scripts/geofile_to_npz.py` | the converter, so the asset is self-contained |  |

The converter stays in the repo, and so do the `.npz` it produced:
`config/sk_geometry.npz`, `config/hk_geometry.npz` and
`config/wcte_geometry.npz` are tracked and are what `lucid/` actually reads.
Nothing in `lucid/` reads a `geofile_*.txt`.
